    "body": "> Yes. In particular, per my bulleted list above, in the success case currently no traversal ever happens. It should happen.\r\n\r\nHmm but if `event.intercept({commit: 'after-transition')` throws when `event.cancelable` is false (or ignores `after-transition`, but that's perhaps too silent), step 32 would commit because the navigation would not have been intercepted, step 37 would return true, and the whole traversal would be committed.\r\nI ran through the algorithm steps and your bullet points a few times and it checks out... Not sure what I'm missing.",
