    "updated_at": "2025-02-20T11:49:35Z",
    "body": "I tried a few things in chrome, it seems like:\r\n- we do the right thing, as in update the actual history entry on commit.\r\n- We do fire popstate (it's probably the right thing to do, in case some existing code relies on those classic events).\r\n\r\nSo I think the right thing to do here is to run the [URL and history update steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#url-and-history-update-steps) 7-11, and also call popstate.\r\nCoincidentally, this is done for fragment navigation: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#navigate-fragid steps 12-14.\r\n\r\nSo I think the plan of action would be to have a few steps equivalent to those fragment-navigation steps, extracting the history length/index from the appropriate places. WDYT @domenic ?\r\n",
